          "senderName": "NWS Anchorage AK",
          "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued October 25 at 3:49PM AKDT until October 25 at 10:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK",
          "description": "* WHAT...Snow expected. Total snow accumulations between 4 and 8\ninches, highest amounts from Paxson north.\n\n* WHERE...Northern Copper Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM AKDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Travel could be very difficult.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Snow will develop across the far northern\nCopper River Valley beginning early this morning. The heaviest snow\nis expected through 4 PM today before slowly tapering off. The best\nchance for accumulating snow will be north of mile post 160 with\nthe highest snow amounts from Paxson north.",
          "instruction": "Slow down and use caution while traveling. For the latest road\nconditions call 5 1 1 or visit 511.alaska.gov.",
          "response": "Execute",
          "note": null,
